-- Distinguish insights actually generated by the AI from everything else.
--
-- WHY: the /ai/insights page showed a "Generated by AI" badge on EVERY card,
-- including the rows written by prisma/seed.ts and seed-insights.ts, which no
-- model ever produced. Under the AI Act transparency work that badge is a
-- disclosure, and putting it on non-AI content states something false. The badge
-- is now driven by this column: shown only when it starts with "ai:".
--
-- VALUES: "ai:<model>" (e.g. "ai:claude-sonnet-5") for rows written by
-- /api/ai/insights/generate; NULL for anything else. Same prefix convention
-- already used by Alert.source ("rule:cashflow_negative").
--
-- SAFETY: this migration only ADDS one nullable column with no default. It drops
-- nothing, renames nothing and rewrites no existing row: every current row simply
-- gets NULL, which reads as "not AI-generated" — exactly the honest answer for
-- the seed rows. Running it on the live database cannot lose data.
--
-- No index on purpose: the column is only read while rendering a page's worth of
-- rows already fetched by organizationId, and an extra index Prisma does not know
-- about would show up as schema drift on the next `prisma migrate dev`.

ALTER TABLE "Insight" ADD COLUMN "source" TEXT;
